course: dictionary
lesson: 7593
title: One word, many meanings: pride
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pride is a word that changes its meaning with the words around it. Read the context to find out which meaning the writer wants. «The Mole, full of lunch and pride, thinks rowing looks easy.» Here pride is not a happy feeling about doing well. The Mole thinks he is better than others, and that makes him too sure of himself.
explain: Ask what the sentence is about. «Pride and truth can live together» is about being proud of something good and honest, not about looking down on people. To check your meaning, swap in a simple word such as "happy feeling about something good" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Pride also appears in phrases. To «take pride in» your work means you care about it and feel good about doing it well. To «swallow your pride» means setting aside your feelings of being too proud, so you can ask for help or say sorry. «Pride comes before a fall» is a saying from old stories, and it warns that being too proud can lead to trouble.
explain: A pride of lions is different. It is a group of lions living together, like a family. Pride can also be a verb: to pride yourself on something means to be proud of it.
fact: Pride has several meanings, so check the context before you choose one.
fact: Healthy pride is the happy feeling you get from effort and achievement, like when you «take pride in» your work.
fact: Pride that makes you look down on others is being too proud, and it can make you unkind.
fact: A pride of lions is a family group of lions living together.
fact: «Pride goes before destruction, a haughty spirit before a fall» is a warning that being too proud can lead to trouble.
exercise: «The Mole, full of lunch and pride, thinks rowing looks easy.» What kind of pride is this? | Happy pride in a good piece of work | Feeling sorry for yourself | A group of animals living together | *Being too proud, thinking you are better than others
exercise: Science class says a pride of lions is a family group. What is a pride of lions? | A kind of bird | A happy feeling after doing well | *A group of lions living together | Someone who thinks they are better than others
exercise: Which phrase means putting aside your pride so you can ask for help? | Pride comes before a fall | *Swallow your pride | Take pride in | Pride of lions
test: In the story «The Emperor's New Clothes», what got in the way of people telling the truth? | Heavy rain | Too much cake | Lost keys | *Pride
test: «The history teacher smiles, because every country tells its story with pride.» What does this mean? | *With a happy feeling about its own story | By looking down on other countries | By giving the story away | By hiding the story from everyone
exam: Jayden says pride is always bad. Is he right? | Yes, pride is always bad | No, pride is only a group of lions | Yes, because pride is a noun | *No, healthy pride is good, but pride that looks down on others can make you unkind
